# MadGraph5 batch script: p p > l+ l- j with the orders stated: QCD=2 QED=2.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   - The stated-order half of the llj pair: exactly two strong and two
#     electroweak couplings, which is what the default selection is claimed to
#     choose for this final state. Holding the generate line fixed and moving
#     only the constraint is what separates an order-semantics error from a
#     diagram-enumeration error.
#   - Its concrete subprocesses are the four banked llj parton rows
#     (u u~ > e+ e- g, d d~ > e+ e- g, g u > e+ e- u, g u~ > e+ e- u~), so the
#     group's amplitude content is claimed there, at per-diagram and per-flow
#     level, rather than here.
#
# Not used for cross sections or event samples: like the default-order script it
# carries a dynamical scale, which the scale layer refuses; pp_to_llj_fixed is
# the same generate line with a fixed-scale run card and is the gated subject.
generate p p > l+ l- j QCD=2 QED=2
output pp_to_llj_qcd2_qed2 -nojpeg
launch
  set ebeam1 6500
  set ebeam2 6500
  done
